commits.message:
feat(windows): stage the CUA driver and enable local control on Windows

Windows packages had no CUA runtime at all, so "This computer" could
never work there: resources/cua-driver.exe and the native SDK were
simply absent from the build, and every win32 path returned
unsupported-platform.

Packaging:
- scripts/prepare-cua-win.mjs stages the checksummed win32 driver and
  SDK outside ASAR (native modules cannot load from an archive);
- electron-builder.yml ships them as cua-driver.exe and cua-sdk/;
- package.json gains build:cua:win and wires it into package:win;
- scripts/smoke-cua-win-embedded.mjs proves a real embedded host
  starts and stops, and runs as a windows-latest CI leg.

Wiring:
- electron/cua.mjs resolves the win32 driver, the standalone named
  pipe, and the embedded host (no TCC prompts to satisfy);
- capabilities.cjs and connectionEnabled report a live Windows
  connection as ready instead of always failing closed;
- startCua runs on win32 at boot, and retry works there too;
- the UI keeps This computer selectable on Windows, like macOS, with a
  message that names the driver instead of a generic failure.
